I am going to check the files in the directory to understand the project structure and context before planning the implementation of the Kudos Wall.I am going to check the files inside prisma, src, and test directories to get a complete view of the files and locate the exact paths.I am going to check the current contents of the prisma/schema.prisma file.I am going to check the current contents of src/modules/index.ts file.I am going to check the CONVENTIONS.md file to understand coding conventions for this scaffold.I am going to check the main Nest application module file.I am going to check test/platform/chassis.test.ts to understand the testing patterns used.[
  {
    "id": "schema-kudos-model",
    "title": "Define Kudos Model in Prisma Schema",
    "goal": "The Kudos model is appended below the MODEL SLOT marker in prisma/schema.prisma. The model has an auto-incrementing integer id as PK, String fields from, to, and message, and a createdAt DateTime field defaulting to now(). Database client generation succeeds successfully.",
    "files_hint": [
      "prisma/schema.prisma"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "prisma-service-module",
    "title": "Implement PrismaService and PrismaModule",
    "goal": "PrismaService extends PrismaClient, implements OnModuleInit, and invokes $connect() on module init in src/modules/prisma/prisma.service.ts. PrismaModule is defined in src/modules/prisma/prisma.module.ts, providing and exporting PrismaService.",
    "files_hint": [
      "src/modules/prisma/prisma.service.ts",
      "src/modules/prisma/prisma.module.ts"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "kudos-service",
    "title": "Implement KudosService",
    "goal": "KudosService in src/modules/kudos/kudos.service.ts is created. Its create method trims fields (from, to, message) and persists via prisma.kudos.create(). Its findAll method returns all records via prisma.kudos.findMany ordered by createdAt desc and id desc.",
    "files_hint": [
      "src/modules/kudos/kudos.service.ts"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "kudos-controller-module-registration",
    "title": "Implement KudosController, KudosModule, and Register KudosModule",
    "goal": "KudosController in src/modules/kudos/kudos.controller.ts is implemented with inline body validation for POST /kudos and getter for GET /kudos. KudosModule compiles in src/modules/kudos/kudos.module.ts importing PrismaModule and registering the controller and service. KudosModule is registered in the MODULES array in src/modules/index.ts.",
    "files_hint": [
      "src/modules/kudos/kudos.controller.ts",
      "src/modules/kudos/kudos.module.ts",
      "src/modules/index.ts"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "kudos-integration-tests",
    "title": "Implement Kudos Integration Tests",
    "goal": "Integration tests are added at test/modules/kudos.spec.ts using @nestjs/testing and vitest globals. Tests comprehensively cover: valid POST 201, whitespace trimming, missing field 400, non-string field 400, empty/whitespace-only field 400, from/to > 100 characters 400, message > 500 characters 400, GET empty 200 [], GET sorted by createdAt desc, and GET tie-breaking by id desc.",
    "files_hint": [
      "test/modules/kudos.spec.ts"
    ]
  }
]
